# Parallel pull requests each insert their entry at the top of an
# `## [Unreleased]` subsection of CHANGELOG.md, so every pair of them conflicts
# on the same few lines. Git's built-in `union` driver resolves such a hunk by
# keeping both sides' lines, ours first, without conflict markers. That is safe
# only while each entry is a self-contained block (one bullet and its indented
# continuation lines): two edits to the SAME existing line are also kept both,
# silently, so review the merged file when a change rewrites an entry.
# GitHub's own mergeability check does not apply this driver; it helps local
# `git merge` and `git rebase` only.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
